---@class hostinger.StartHostingWebsiteSetupV1Request
---@field order_id number Hosting order ID. List orders to find available IDs.
---@field type? hostinger.StartHostingWebsiteSetupV1RequestType|string|distilled.Null Website type. Omit or `null` for an empty website. `wordpress` installs WordPress in the website root and requires `wordpress`. The headless types (`headless_empty`, `headless_wordpress`, `headless_ecommerce`, `headless_pocketbase`) create a headless website; `headless_wordpress` additionally installs WordPress into the `cms` directory with generated credentials. `headless_empty` installs nothing, so WordPress can be added later through `POST /api/hosting/v1/accounts/{username}/wordpress/installations` (`wordpress_installations_install`) with `type: headless`.
---@field domain? string|distilled.Null Customer-owned domain. Omit or `null` to set the website up on a generated temporary free subdomain. Cannot start with "www." and can have at most one subdomain level, e.g. `blog.example.com`. A free subdomain generated through `POST /api/hosting/v1/domains/free-subdomains` in the last 24 hours is also accepted.
---@field datacenter_code? string|distilled.Null Datacenter for the hosting account when the order does not have one yet. Omit to use the order's default datacenter. Ignored when the order already has a hosting account. List available datacenters to find valid codes.
---@field wordpress? hostinger.StartHostingWebsiteSetupV1RequestWordpress|distilled.Null WordPress install settings. Required when `type` is `wordpress`, not allowed otherwise. The site title is the domain.

