---Get website
---
---Get the link for the user to open their website in Hostinger Horizons interface.\n
---Use this tool when the user wants the link to an existing website, or when you need its
---website URL before or after editing it.\n
---`is_in_progress` is true while changes are being generated or the website is being published;
---wait until it is false before publishing. `published_at` is when the website was last published,
---`is_template` is whether its published pages show the "Use template" banner, and
---`has_ecommerce_store` is whether it has an online store.\n
---Websites can be edited with the `Edit website` tool, or by the user in Hostinger Horizons
---interface in the provided website URL.
---
---`GET /api/horizons/v1/websites/{websiteId}`
---@param input hostinger.GetHorizonWebsiteV1Request
---@return hostinger.HorizonsV1WebsitesWebsiteUrlResource? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_horizon_website_v1(input) end

---Show AI option status
---
---Show the current AI option status for the Hostinger Tools plugin on the
---specified WordPress installation. Filter by `option` to return a single
---option, or omit it to return all options.
---
---Provide the WordPress installation (software) identifier in the path. It can
---be obtained from GET /api/hosting/v1/wordpress/installations (the `id` field).
---
---`GET /api/hosting/v1/accounts/{username}/wordpress/{software}/hostinger-plugins/ai-option/status`
---@param input hostinger.GetHostingAIOptionStatusV1Request
---@return hostinger.WordPressV1HostingerPluginsAiOptionStatusResource? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_hosting_ai_option_status_v1(input) end

---Get cache status
---
---Returns the caching state of the website: whether server-side caching is enabled and whether
---development (cacheless) mode is on. Works for the main domain, addon websites, parked domains
---and subdomains of the account; each reports its own settings and does not inherit them from
---its parent website.
---
---`is_enabled` is the setting changed by `Toggle website cache` and reflects a toggle
---immediately. `is_cacheless_mode_enabled` is true while development mode is on; caching is then
---bypassed even when `is_enabled` is true. `Toggle cacheless mode` is applied in the background,
---so this flag can take a few minutes to follow it.
---
---The domain must be the exact website name as listed on the account, without a `www.` prefix.
---Returns 404 when the domain is not a website on the account.
---
---`GET /api/hosting/v1/accounts/{username}/websites/{domain}/cache/status`
---@param input hostinger.GetHostingCacheStatusV1Request
---@return hostinger.HostingV1CacheCacheStatusResource? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_hosting_cache_status_v1(input) end

---Get CDN status
---
---Returns whether the Hostinger CDN is enabled for the website domain. Works for the main
---domain, parked domains and subdomains of the account.
---
---The domain must be the exact website name as listed on the account, without a `www.` prefix.
---Returns 404 when the domain is not a website on the account.
---
---`GET /api/hosting/v1/accounts/{username}/websites/{domain}/cdn/status`
---@param input hostinger.GetHostingCDNStatusV1Request
---@return hostinger.HostingV1CdnCdnStatusResource? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_hosting_cdn_status_v1(input) end

